{"timestamp": "2026-08-09T17:13:02.328809+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a5c32b92-0828-4df3-9041-31098c7e9dbd', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You write one already-planned educational page object.\\n\\nYou may not change:\\n- block ID;\\n- section ID;\\n- position;\\n- pedagogical intent;\\n- requested object type;\\n- lesson objective;\\n- scope restrictions.\\n\\nYour output is the content object only. It must validate against the supplied form schema. Do not wrap it in markdown, explanation, or an object-name envelope.\\n\\nRespect:\\n- grade level;\\n- terminology;\\n- must-not-introduce constraints;\\n- neighboring block summaries;\\n- the specific pedagogical intent;\\n- the block brief.\\n\\nDo not invent answers inside student question content. Assessment answers are returned only through the assessment bundle contract.\\n\\nReturn JSON only for the selected content schema.\\n\\n\\n## INPUT JSON\\n{\\n  \"block\": {\\n    \"brief\": \"Provide several organisms: sunflower, apple tree, grass, cow, mushroom, caterpillar. Ask students to sort into producers and consumers, explaining the rule: a producer makes its own food via photosynthesis; a consumer eats other living things. Clarify that making fruits is not the definition\\\\u2014grass is a producer that makes no fruits, yet it still makes its own food.\",\\n    \"id\": \"contrast-b2\",\\n    \"intent\": \"classify\",\\n    \"object\": \"list\",\\n    \"placement\": \"main\",\\n    \"position\": 1\\n  },\\n  \"lesson_context\": {\\n    \"anchor\": {\\n      \"description\": \"A sunflower in a pot on a windowsill, growing tall and healthy without ever being fed anything but\\\\u2026\",\\n      \"id\": \"anchor-1\"\\n    },\\n    \"grade_level\": \"Grade 4\",\\n    \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n      \"Detailed chemical equations (e.g., 6CO\\\\u2082 + 6H\\\\u2082O \\\\u2192 C\\\\u2086H\\\\u2081\\\\u2082O\\\\u2086 + 6O\\\\u2082)\",\\n      \"Cellular respiration\",\\n      \"Chloroplast structure at the molecular level\",\\n      \"Light-dependent and light-independent reactions\",\\n      \"Quantitative limiting factors\"\\n    ],\\n    \"objective\": \"Identify that plants are producers because they make their own food, unlike animals that eat other living things.\",\\n    \"subject\": \"Science\"\\n  },\\n  \"neighbours\": {\\n    \"after\": \"Present this scenario: A student says, \\'The sunflower grew because it took food from the soil through its roots.\\' Then ask: \\'If that were true, what would happen if we grew a sunflower in plain sand with no nutrients but lots of light? Use what you learned to decide if the student is right and explain why.\\' Provide a prompt that targets the specific error.\",\\n    \"before\": \"Compare the sunflower (makes its own food using light) with a rabbit (must eat grass to get energy and building materials). Highlight that the rabbit is a consumer, the sunflower a producer. The rabbit\\'s food comes from the sunflower, but the sunflower\\'s food comes from its own manufacturing.\"\\n  },\\n  \"section_context\": {\\n    \"section_id\": \"contrast\"\\n  },\\n  \"terminology\": [\\n    \"producer\",\\n    \"photosynthesis\",\\n    \"chlorophyll\",\\n    \"carbon dioxide\",\\n    \"oxygen\",\\n    \"sugar\"\\n  ],\\n  \"writer_contract\": {\\n    \"capacity\": {\\n      \"itemsMax\": 8,\\n      \"itemsMin\": 3,\\n      \"leadInMaxWords\": 20,\\n      \"wordsPerItem\": 25\\n    },\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"content_schema\": {\\n      \"items\": \"ListItem[]\",\\n      \"lead_in\": \"RichText|null\",\\n      \"style\": \"ordered|unordered|steps|glossary\"\\n    },\\n    \"failure_examples\": [],\\n    \"generation_guidance\": \"\",\\n    \"object_id\": \"list\",\\n    \"object_validation\": []\\n  }\\n}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': \"Return JSON only for this block's content schema.\"}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'stream': False}}"}
